  "_doc": "The editorial rubric.\n\nDESIGN NOTE (learned the hard way on the 2026-09-03 run): money figures and HN engagement must NEVER qualify a story on their own. The first version let them, and the queue filled with an Nvidia acquisition, a humanoid-robot launch, and a dark-matter detector -- all big numbers, none of them about compute costing somebody something. Category match is now a GATE. Everything else is a booster applied on top.\n\nStrong terms are self-qualifying: one hit means the story is plausibly ours. Weak terms are generic ('outage', 'complexity', 'capex') and need a second hit to count, because on their own they match half the tech press.",
